===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|arhwō|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|h₂érkʷo-||bow, arrow|lang=ine-pro}}. Near cognates include Gothic {{term|𐌰𐍂𐍈𐌰𐌶𐌽𐌰|tr=arƕazna|lang=got}} and Old Norse {{term|ǫr|lang=non}}; further cognates include Latin {{term|arcus||bow|lang=la}}.

